  "id": "COMPOUND:14975 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Aloesol is implicated in the interaction with SNB-78 through a series of molecular pathways, with Carboxylesterase 2 and Maplexin A acting as intermediaries. The evidence suggests that Aloesol targets Carboxylesterase 2, which is then targeted by two distinct compounds: (7E,9E,16Z)-18-hydroxyoctadeca-7,9,16-trien-11,13-diyn-4-one and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. Both of these compounds share a common target, SNB-78, indicating a potential mechanism where Aloesol indirectly influences SNB-78 through the activation of these target molecules. The presence of multiple pathways converging on SNB-78 suggests a complex regulatory network, possibly involving the modulation of enzyme activity or signaling pathways. The integration of these findings highlights the role of Aloesol in orchestrating interactions that ultimately affect SNB-78, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
